  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no new independent validation was released or requested; independent validation capacity remains exhausted, so the synthesis stage consolidates discovery evidence and prioritizes the already registered decomposition analyses. I reassess and accept H238/R228: the formally reversed feature_010-by-feature_038 interaction is supported, signed +0.812 [0.643, 0.981] composite dependency-score units in the claimed negative direction. Because H231 tested the opposite claimed positive interaction and was rejected, this should be read as dataset-specific evidence that the feature_010 contrast is much less positive, and plausibly negative, among high feature_038 than among low feature_038. The simple high/low effects and whether the pattern persists when feature_063=1 individuals are excluded remain to be characterized by H239-H241 and the newly registered feature_063=0 simple effects. The central supported association remains that feature_063=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency primarily when feature_038 is high. The broad interaction is signed +0.559 [0.387, 0.731] (H200/R195), the high-feature_038 simple effect is +0.529 [0.395, 0.664] (H212/R207), and the clean anchor-negative interaction/simple effects are +0.576 [0.461, 0.691] (H217/R213) and +0.568 [0.466, 0.669] (H215/R211). Threshold and band analyses support a robust positive feature_038 region rather than a single cutoff artifact: feature_038>=0.5 +0.501 [0.333, 0.669] (H223/R219), >=1.0 +0.514 [0.267, 0.761] (H224/R220), intermediate 0.5 to 1.0 +0.494 [0.257, 0.730] (H233/R230), and 0 to 0.5 +0.580 [0.350, 0.809] (H226/R223). Low and near-zero feature_038 strata are null or reject the negative-direction claim: signed -0.029 [-0.138, 0.079] for feature_038<=0 (H213/R208), -0.008 [-0.062, 0.046] in clean anchors (H216/R212), and -0.083 [-0.224, 0.059] at feature_038<=-0.5 (H225/R221). The overall feature_063 main effect is accepted but modest and less threshold-decisive than the conditional effect: discovery signed +0.227 [0.131, 0.323] (H44/R45) and validation signed +0.290 [0.143, 0.437] (R52), with lower bounds near 0.15. Among the constructed continuous assays, feature_036 is neither necessary nor sufficient to explain the feature_038 modification: the high-feature_038 feature_063 effect persists when feature_036 is high (+0.466 [0.259, 0.673], H228/R225) and when it is low (+0.591 [0.413, 0.768], H229/R226), while the feature_036-by-feature_063 interaction screen is unsupported (-0.137 [-0.330, 0.055], H202/R197). feature_018 is not required; the high-feature_038 effect is very large when feature_018<=0 (+0.818 [0.739, 0.897], H220/R216) and the corresponding conditional interaction is supported (+0.790 [0.562, 1.018], H222/R218). When feature_018>=0, the simple effect remains above threshold but smaller (+0.324 [0.176, 0.473], H219/R215), and a cleaner conditional interaction is supported (+0.352 [0.180, 0.524], H234/R231), whereas the broader feature_018 interaction screen remains unresolved. Specificity checks show the feature_038 modification is not a generic modifier of every accepted predictor: H230 rejects positive feature_038 modification of feature_002, H232 rejects negative feature_038 modification of feature_027, and clean-anchor feature_038 modification of feature_037 is unsupported (-0.055 [-0.124, 0.015], H218/R214). Nevertheless, the feature_063-by-feature_038 association persists within feature_037=1 (+0.589 [0.269, 0.909], H237/R234), and the corresponding feature_002=1 interaction is directionally strong but borderline unresolved (+0.483 [0.143, 0.822], H236/R233), prompting the registered simple feature_002=1 high/low feature_038 contrasts H242-H243. The accepted main-effect landscape is feature_002=1 associated with weaker dependency (+0.831 [0.766, 0.897], H47/R23), feature_010=1 associated with weaker dependency (+0.423 [0.327, 0.520], H25/R40) but with strong high-feature_038 effect modification, feature_037=1 associated with stronger dependency (+0.833 [0.767, 0.898], H30/R42), feature_027=1 associated with stronger dependency (+0.792 [0.676, 0.907], H115/R122; validated +0.826 [0.635, 1.017], R128), and feature_063=1 associated with modestly stronger dependency overall but markedly stronger at high feature_038. Negative or unsupported findings include no meaningful effects for the constructed binary assays feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015, including validated feature_058 null/rejection (H5/R5/R76), no robust threshold-supported effect for feature_003 after validation or stringent anchoring (H39/R21/R25; H122/R97/R101), no robust feature_031 effect (H23/R17; H62/R31/R102), broad null feature_053 contrasts (H33/H34/H175/H176), and most tested categorical contrasts or interactions. Invalid sparse-cell comparisons remain unresolved and are not evidence of absence. These conclusions are associations among measured predictors in the supplied dataset. The outcome is a composite dependency score, predictors are opaque or constructed assays, and there is no evidence for causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability. The most informative next analysis is to decompose the reversed feature_010-by-feature_038 interaction and the borderline feature_002=1 feature_063 modification: prioritize H239-H243 and the newly registered feature_010 simple effects among feature_063=0 at high and low feature_038.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 21 synthesis update. Validation budget is exhausted; no due validation responses. H238/R228 accepted active: reversed feature_010-by-feature_038 interaction signed +0.812 [0.643,0.981], meaning feature_010 association is much weaker/more negative among high feature_038; pending H239-H241 and new simple feature_010 feature_063=0 analyses to distinguish genuine modification from feature_063 confounding. Central accepted heterogeneity: feature_063 stronger-dependency association is concentrated at high feature_038 (broad interaction +0.559 [0.387,0.731], high simple +0.529 [0.395,0.664], clean interaction +0.576 [0.461,0.691], simple +0.568 [0.466,0.669]); low feature_038 simple claims rejected/near null. Overall feature_063 main effect accepted but near threshold by lower bounds (discovery +0.227 [0.131,0.323], validation +0.290 [0.143,0.437]); conditional high-feature_038 evidence is stronger. feature_036 does not explain feature_038 modification; feature_018 is not required but conditioning reveals stronger high-feature_038 effect when feature_018<=0 and smaller but supported when feature_018>=0. feature_038 modification is not generic: rejected for feature_002/feature_027 registered directions, unsupported clean-anchor feature_037 interaction, but accepted within feature_037=1 for feature_063; feature_002=1 feature_063 interaction borderline unresolved (+0.483 [0.143,0.822]), pending H242-H243. Main accepted associations: feature_002=1 weaker dependency, feature_010=1 weaker dependency overall, feature_037=1 stronger, feature_027=1 stronger (validated), feature_063=1 modest stronger. Null/rejected: feature_007, feature_058 validated, feature_015, feature_003 validation/strengthened anchors, feature_031, broad feature_053, most categorical contrasts. Sparse invalid cells remain unresolved. No causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims. Active plan: analyze H239-H243 and new feature_010 simple effects within feature_063=0; then decide whether reversed feature_010 effect is independent of feature_063 and whether feature_002=1 interaction has meaningful high/low simple contrasts."
